@ENDNODE
@NODE INSTALL "Install or update"
Requires AmigaOS 3.2, 68020+, a compatible bsdsocket.library TCP/IP stack,
and AmiSSL 5.1 or newer for HTTPS. ReAction and picture datatypes come from
AmigaOS. Additional image formats may require suitable picture datatypes.

Extract the complete archive and double-click Install. Novice mode locates an
existing installation automatically and offers Update or Uninstall. A fresh
installation uses SYS:Utilities for the client and SYS:Prefs for
AmiRocketPrefs, without directory prompts. Intermediate and Expert modes
allow separate application and Preferences drawers. Expert mode also allows
a drawer for the single AmiRocket.prefs configuration file. Close the
client and Preferences before updating. Shared resources use SYS:AmiRocket;
Expert mode can select another dedicated shared-data drawer. The manual is
installed directly in HELP:.
Application locations are recorded in the selected AmiRocket.prefs file.
A small OS environment locator AmiRocket-ConfigFile holds only its filename.
All client, Preferences and plugin settings remain in the same file.

Updates preserve ENVARC:AmiRocket.prefs, custom icons and unrelated plugins.
The installer never imports account settings from a distribution archive.
Launch AmiRocket from its Workbench icon. Per-server auto-connect preferences
decide which servers connect when the client starts.

Shell installation: CD to the extracted AmiRocket drawer, then execute:
 Execute scripts/Install-AmiRocket DEST=SYS:Utilities DATA=SYS:AmiRocket

Shell launch: Stack 65536, then AmiRocket. Workbench icons request this stack.
All three user levels offer Update / Uninstall when an installation is found;
otherwise a fresh installation is performed. Use Install in the extracted
release archive for maintenance.
The installer launcher and Shell script are not copied into the installed app.
After installation, a summary lists the client, Preferences and configuration
paths on Installer's final page, without an Abort Install button. A setup option
starts AmiRocket once after success; it creates no startup entry.
Uninstall removes both executables from their selected drawers and offers
Keep settings or Remove settings for the selected shared configuration file.

@ENDNODE
@NODE USE "Using AmiRocket"
Installation selects the bundled notification chime automatically, including
updates from the old blank setting. Custom sound choices are preserved.
Preferences / Notifications selects a sound file and provides a Test sound
button. Blank uses the system beep. Custom sounds use installed sound datatypes
(for example 8SVX), are limited to 256 KiB, and are cached. Enable sounds per
server in Servers / Edit. Quiet mode and mention-only rules still apply.
The installer lets every user level set the default download drawer, starting
with SYS:Downloads. Intermediate/Expert also choose the media cache drawer.
Both paths can be changed later in Preferences / Helpers.

Attachment cards show a shortened filename and size. Preview/Hide loads or
collapses a thumbnail. Open uses the configured external image viewer; Save
chooses a destination. Loading and failures stay on the card; use Retry after
failure. Cached thumbnails reopen without downloading or decoding again.
General preferences: disable thumbnail previews for text-only cards; enable
Load visible thumbnails automatically for one-at-a-time server thumbnails.
The default is click-to-load. Automatic mode never downloads originals and
is disabled in low-memory mode. Default preview bounds are 320 by 180 pixels.

Add servers in AmiRocketPrefs. Right-click a server to connect, disconnect,
or edit it. Select its root for connection events and failures.

Enter sends a message. Shift+Enter inserts a new line. Amiga+C/X/V provide
clipboard editing. Select a received message and Amiga+C copies its text.
Amiga+U selects the next unread room; Amiga+L jumps to the new-message marker.
Unread rooms are bold; @ badges indicate mentions. Room history uses WebSocket-triggered delta sync with polling fallback.

Attachments display server-reported sizes. Click an image to expand it or
use Room / Save selected attachment to save. Unsupported previews offer Save.
Downloads are limited to 8 MiB, previews to 2 MiB and one million pixels.
Cancellation may wait for the current network read, up to 30 seconds.

If delivery is unconfirmed, check the conversation before resending. AmiRocket
never automatically replays a message after a lost response. Drafts are kept.
Project / Iconify (Amiga+H) keeps connections active behind a Workbench icon.
Server roots and the header show health and retry countdowns. Click a server
root for the detailed connection-event history.

Room / Search this conversation (Amiga+F), or Find, searches up to 25 results per
page. Select a result to read/copy its text. Previous/Next page through hits.
File, or Room / Upload attachment, streams a file up to 8 MiB with progress
and cancellation. The selected file is sent separately; composer text remains
a draft. Check the chat before retrying an unconfirmed upload.

Drafts checkpoint every two seconds and on conversation/server switches.
AmiRocket.drafts in the shared-data drawer contains private recovery data for up to 64 private draft/delivery records,
scoped to server/account/conversation. It is not a configuration file and is
never packaged. Updates preserve it. Close the client before deleting it.
Failed disk writes keep data in memory; an unsafe switch is blocked.
Drag the horizontal divider above the input to resize it. The client
remembers its height in AmiRocket.prefs alongside your window settings.

Right-click a message or select it and press Amiga+T for message actions.
Quote inserts text into your draft. Load thread shows paged replies.
Reply in thread sends the separate editor's text to that thread. Select a
reply to act on it. Load for editing copies your own selected message;
Save edit submits it. Delete own message requires confirmation. Reaction
shortcodes such as smile have explicit Add and Remove buttons.
Workspace permissions and edit/delete time limits still apply. Failed or
unconfirmed actions retain their text and are never automatically retried.

AmiRocketPrefs > Servers > Edit offers per-server mentions-only alerts,
notification beep/flash and Quiet mode. Quiet mode keeps unread badges
while suppressing message alerts and message events to plugins/docks.
Use applies immediately; Save also writes the same configuration file.
Restart client and Preferences after installing an updated build.

Image previews use the server's image URL; Save attachment retains the
original file URL. Enable Rocket.Chat server thumbnails (480x360 is suitable).
Preferences > General > Preview width accepts 160, 320 or 640. Low-memory
mode caps previews at 160x120. Images retain their aspect ratio. Use applies
immediately; Save also persists this in the shared preferences file.
Previews are cached in memory for reopening. A missing server thumbnail still
requires the original to fit the existing memory and format limits.

Full-size images open externally by default. Set the program in Preferences
> Helpers > Image viewer executable (default SYS:Utilities/MultiView).
With Open full-size images in external viewer enabled, click an expanded
thumbnail to open its original without a Save requester. Image labels toggle
server thumbnails; if no separate thumbnail exists, the original opens outside.
Room > Open selected image externally also opens the selected original.

Originals are not decoded in AmiRocket. Up to four temporary originals share
an 8 MiB budget (2 MiB in low-memory mode); cached originals reopen without
another download. Files remain in T: while viewers may need them, including
after the client exits. Close viewers before Room > Clear temporary image
files. Use Save attachment when you want to choose a permanent location.

@ENDNODE
@NODE PREFS "Preferences and plugins"
Launch AmiRocketPrefs from SYS:Prefs or from the client menu. Use applies settings for this session;
Save also writes the selected AmiRocket.prefs file. It is the single configuration file
for servers, appearance, performance, helpers and plugin options.

Network enables realtime WebSocket event subscriptions by default.
Disable Realtime WebSocket updates for polling only. Live events coalesce
into delta syncs; periodic catch-up handles missed events. Lost streams
reconnect with backoff; sends are never automatically replayed.
Network sets a per-server request gap (default 1000 ms), idle polling (30s)
and a 24-hour avatar disk cache. Use applies now; Save also keeps these values.
Room lists refresh at most every 30s, foreground presence every 60s. Hidden
or idle conversations poll less often. Searches and name suggestions are local.
429/503 Retry-After pauses all requests to that server; failures back off with
jitter. User actions have priority over avatar/presence work; sends are never
replayed automatically. Disconnect cancels queued operations.
Diagnostics / Refresh network statistics shows requests/min, queue, cooldown,
last HTTP status, errors, rate limits and cache hits (sampled every 5 seconds).
Avatar cache: PROGDIR:Cache/Avatars, up to 8 MiB image data in 64 slots.
Disable caching or delete that drawer to clear it. Configuration stays in the
single preferences file; cache entries are not settings.

Remember login saves an authentication token, never the password. Log out and
forget login revokes the token. Do not share your personal configuration file.

Memory sets chat retention (50-1000 messages per server) and encoded image
cache size (256-8192 KiB). Low-memory mode caps retention at 200, disables
avatar downloads and emoji drawing, keeps two previews / 512 KiB encoded data,
and limits downloads to 2 MiB. Room / Clear media caches clears RAM media and
the disk avatar cache where writable. Use applies now; Save also persists.

Timestamp and Quick Reply are bundled, disabled unless explicitly enabled.
The separately distributed plugin SDK contains headers, source examples and
ARexx scripts. SDK and example licences/notices accompany their source.
@ENDNODE
@NODE REXX "ARexx and dock integration"
The public port is AMIROCKET (additional clients use AMIROCKET.2 etc.).
HELP and CAPABILITIES describe commands. STATUS, DOCKSTATUS and SERVERSTATUS
supply state. SHOW, ICONIFY and CONNECT/DISCONNECT allow dock control.
Version 2 subscriptions carry epoch/sequence/drop metadata for recovery.

AmiRocketMonitor is the native receiver example. Shell: Stack 65536, then
AmiRocketMonitor. Ctrl-C exits. Rexx/ contains ready-to-adapt scripts.
A real NovaDock widget still needs its own integration and rendering tests.
@ENDNODE
@NODE REMOVE "Uninstall"
From an extracted release drawer, double-click Install. Novice mode locates
the installed AmiRocket drawer and offers Update or Uninstall.
Uninstall then offers Keep settings (default) or Remove settings. The installer removes
only its known managed files and any owned startup entry from older installers.

Keep settings preserves the selected AmiRocket.prefs file. Remove settings deletes this
shared file and the old ENV fallback, including all saved server tokens and
plugin options for every installation. Unrelated files/plugins are always kept.
The drawer may remain when custom files are present. To forget accounts, use Log out and
forget login before uninstalling. You may remove the saved configuration
manually if you no longer want it. Updates never delete this file.
@ENDNODE
@NODE SOURCE "Licence and corresponding source"
AmiRocket: GPL-3.0-or-later, copyright 2026 Tommy Froessman and contributors.
See LICENSE and COPYRIGHT. Beam68-derived release tools retain their MIT
notice in licenses/Beam68-release-tools.txt.

The Source drawer in the runtime archive and the versioned source ZIP contain the
corresponding source, Makefile, SDK, release scripts and regression tests.
README.md and docs/RELEASING.md document rebuilding. VERSION identifies this
release; BUILD-PROVENANCE.json records exact native input/output hashes.

@ENDNODE
@NODE CONTROLS "Recovery, navigation and low-resource controls"
Release 0.2 controls:
 First unread: explicitly load older history to the read boundary, bounded by
 the configured message limit. Escape stops further history paging.
 Ctrl+Tab / Ctrl+Shift+Tab: next / previous visible conversation.
 Ctrl+K: search conversations; Enter opens the first match.
 Ctrl+U: next unread conversation. Escape closes secondary windows.

Failed composer sends keep their draft and delivery ID in private recovery data.
Retry send checks delivery before reusing the original ID. Recovery survives a
restart; there is no automatic replay. Editing an unconfirmed draft asks before
using a new ID. Room / Forget unconfirmed delivery keeps the text but discards
its ID after confirmation; check history first to avoid a duplicate new send.

Memory / Use low-resource preset stages smaller caches and previews, fewer
retained messages, disabled automatic images/avatars/emoji and slower polling.
Use or Save applies it without changing server accounts or custom drawers.
Diagnostics / Copy diagnostic report copies counters and fixed diagnoses without
credentials, URLs or message text. Transfers show speed and ETA when known;
Escape cancels the transfer. Short action feedback appears in the chat header.

@ENDNODE
